    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, traced through the actual code.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n**A. Framework-level, before the controller body runs**\n\n1. **JSON deserialization** \u2192 `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n2. **Bean Validation on the DTO** (`@Valid` on the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` parameter). Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Size(4..4)` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (optional)\n   - Failure \u2192 **400** (via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n3. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Failure \u2192 **403**.\n\n**B. Manual checks inside `addOwner`, in this exact order**\n\n4. Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; `id` and `pets` ignored).\n5. **`normalizeNewOwner(owner)`** runs a sequence, any failure \u2192 **400**:\n   - a. `normalizeAddress` \u2014 reject if address blank (also expands ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n   - b. `toE164(telephone)` \u2014 reject if telephone can't be converted to E.164 (validates national-number length: AU +61 \u2192 9 digits, NANP +1 \u2192 10).\n   - c. lower-case the email.\n   - d. `postcodeValidForCity` \u2014 postcode must be 4 digits and fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) when the region is known.\n   - e. default `registrationDate` to today if null.\n   - f. `rollToBusinessDay` \u2014 Sat/Sun rolled forward to Monday.\n6. **`dailyLimitReached(registrationDate)`** \u2014 \u2265100 owners already on that registration date \u2192 **429**.\n7. **`cityIsAtCapacity(city)`** \u2014 \u226550 owners already in that city \u2192 **409**.\n8. **`identityKeyAlreadyUsed(owner)`** \u2014 duplicate identity key \u2192 **409**. (Note: this check runs *after* the possible household save in step 11 below.)\n\n> Order caveat: household lookup/join (side-effect #11) happens *between* the capacity checks and the identity-key check \u2014 see side-effects list.\n\n**C. Entity-level Bean Validation at flush/commit (second pass)**\n\n9. When the transaction commits, Hibernate re-validates the `Owner`/`Person` entity constraints: `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty`, `address` `@NotEmpty`, `city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`, `email` `@Email`. A DB `DataIntegrityViolationException` surfaces as **404** via the advice.\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\n1. **Household join (conditional):** `findHouseholdMember` \u2192 if a match exists *and* `sharesHousehold` is true, `joinHousehold` derives a deterministic `householdId` and **saves the existing owner** (`clinicService.saveOwner(existing)`) \u2014 an extra DB write to a *different* row during creation.\n2. **Derived fields set on the new owner** (pure in-memory, but computed via repeated full-table reads `findAllOwners()`):\n   - `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`\n   - `namesakeCount`\n   - `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`\n   - `bulkSignupWarning` (true when >80 signups that day)\n   - `householdSize`\n3. **Persist the new owner:** `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `@Transactional` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (insert; assigns generated `id`).\n4. **Audit log line:** `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...\")`.\n5. **Transaction commit** \u2192 Hibernate flush (entity validation from step 9, then DB write).\n6. **Response:** map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 Created**.\n\n**Not present on this path:** no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist` or `@EntityListeners`, no application events/`@EventListener`, no emails, no messaging, no cache eviction. The only writes are the two `saveOwner` calls (the conditional existing-owner update and the new-owner insert) plus the audit log line.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: in the **jdbc** profile, the repository's update branch only writes `first_name, last_name, address, city, telephone`, so the household-join update (side-effect #1) would not persist `householdId` and the other extended columns on the existing owner under that profile."
